    {
      "filename": "A photo booth on Penang Hill (12253939185).jpg",
      "title": "File:A photo booth on Penang Hill (12253939185).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/24/A_photo_booth_on_Penang_Hill_%2812253939185%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_photo_booth_on_Penang_Hill_(12253939185).jpg",
      "width": 4288,
      "height": 2848,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "shankar s. from Dubai, united arab emirates",
      "description": "This is becoming a cliche at every major tourist attraction everywhere in the world nowadays: a photo booth where you get your photograph taken. This picture is then given to you as a print, or mounted on a t-shirt, coffee mug, keychain and stuff. This is the one on Penang Hill, and you can see a picture of the funicular clearly in the background. Several folks were crowding intothe photo booth. The only good thing here is, while some volunteers are at times aggressive and irritatingly pushy, trying to push their photo services, (Jurong Bird Park, Singapore and Ocean Park HK  spring to mind), here no one was soliciting and there were no pesky volunteers around. (Georgetown, Penang, Malaysia, Nov. 2013)",
      "dateCreated": "2013-11-01 00:00",
